# .html duplicates of the clean URLs — Netlify serves BOTH variants with a 200.
# Canonicals cover the indexable pages; these 301s stop inbound links being spent
# on the wrong variant. The "!" is required — Netlify ignores a redirect whose source
# matches a real file in the publish dir unless it is forced. Verified: forcing does NOT
# re-enter the clean-URL resolver, so /x still serves 200 with zero redirects.
/index.html                      /                             301!
